{"page":"RAP1GDS1","gene":"RAP1GDS1","accession":"P52306","protein":"Rap1 GTPase-GDP dissociation stimulator 1","length":607,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"P52306-1","name":"1","synonyms":["SmgGDS-607"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Acts as a GEF (guanine nucleotide exchange factor) for unprenylated RHOA (PubMed:24415755, PubMed:28630045, PubMed:30190425). Chaperones the entry and passage of small GTPases through the prenylation pathway (PubMed:20709748). Recognizes the last amino acid in the GTPase C-terminal CAAX motif with a preference for 'Leu' over 'Met', indicating involvement in the geranylgeranylation pathway (PubMed:24415755)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts with unprenylated RHOA; the interaction is direct (PubMed:20709748, PubMed:28630045, PubMed:30190425). Interacts with RAP1A (PubMed:20709748). Interacts with KRAS (PubMed:20709748, PubMed:24415755). Interacts with RAC1 (PubMed:20709748). Interacts with RAP1B (PubMed:24415755). Preferentially interacts with unprenylated GTPases that will become geranylgeranylated (PubMed:24415755). May also interact with prenylated GTPases (PubMed:24415755)"}],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000408927.8"],"refseq":["NM_001100427.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001093897.1"],"maneSelect":true},"model":{"entry":"AF-P52306-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P52306-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":95.5,"plddt":[[0,1],[50,1],[70,13],[50,5],[70,5],[90,35],[70,1],[90,1],[70,1],[90,147],[70,4],[90,21],[70,1],[90,135],[70,2],[90,83],[70,1],[90,146],[70,2],[50,2]]}},"features":[{"type":"Site","start":1,"end":2,"description":"Breakpoint for translocation to form the NUP98-RAP1GDS1 fusion protein"},{"type":"Motif","start":4,"end":13,"description":"Nuclear export signal (NES)"},{"type":"Repeat","start":89,"end":131,"description":"ARM 1"},{"type":"Region","start":122,"end":170,"description":"Prevents binding to prenylated RHOA"},{"type":"Repeat","start":170,"end":211,"description":"ARM 2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":230,"end":230,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Region","start":239,"end":255,"description":"Interacts with polybasic regions in GTPases"},{"type":"Repeat","start":347,"end":390,"description":"ARM 3"},{"type":"Region","start":379,"end":428,"description":"Critical for catalytic activity"},{"type":"Repeat","start":391,"end":431,"description":"ARM 4"},{"type":"Repeat","start":479,"end":519,"description":"ARM 5"}],"interfaces":{},"isoforms":[{"accession":"P52306-2","name":"2","synonyms":["SmgGDS-558"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Acts as a GEF (guanine nucleotide exchange factor) for prenylated RHOA (PubMed:21242305, PubMed:28630045, PubMed:30190425). Acts as a GEF for RHOC (PubMed:21242305). Chaperones the downstream trafficking and/or processing of small newly prenylated GTPases (PubMed:20709748). Escorts RAC1 to the nucleus (PubMed:12551911)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts with prenylated RHOA; the interaction is direct and in a 1:1 stoichiometry (PubMed:12551911, PubMed:20709748, PubMed:28630045, PubMed:30190425). Interacts with RAP1A (PubMed:20709748). Interacts with KRAS (PubMed:20709748, PubMed:24415755). Interacts with RAC1 (PubMed:12551911, PubMed:20709748). Interacts with RAP1B (PubMed:24415755). Preferentially interacts with prenylated GTPases (PubMed:24415755)"}],"length":558,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000408900.7"],"refseq":["NM_001100429.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001093899.1"],"maneSelect":false},"segments":[[1,1,121],[122,171,437]],"edits":[{"start":122,"end":170,"original":"EGRSAVDQAGGAQIVIDHLRSLCSITDPANEKLLTVFCGM","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":49,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":49,"foldedMissing":49,"features":[[2,10,0],[3,49,0],[4,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-P52306-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P52306-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":95.3,"plddt":[[0,1],[50,1],[70,14],[50,4],[70,5],[90,35],[70,3],[90,55],[70,3],[90,1],[70,1],[90,38],[70,4],[